<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving simultaneous equations of a given line and parabola.</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the simultaneous equations \[ y = {@line@}, \qquad y = {@para@}. \]</p>
<p>Give your \(x\)-values in the form \([x_1, x_2]\) and the corresponding \(y\)-values as \([y_1, y_2]\). Type <code>sqrt(3)</code> for \(\sqrt{3}\).</p>
<div>\(x\)-values: \(= \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>Corresponding \(y\)-values: \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>At a solution, both equations give the <strong>same value of \(y\)</strong>, so we equate the right-hand sides and solve the resulting quadratic in \(x\):</p>
\[ \begin{align*} {@para@} &= {@line@}\\ {@quadexpr@} &= 0. \end{align*} \]
<p>This does not factorise. Using the quadratic formula with \(a = 1\), \(b = {@-2*hh@}\), \(c = {@hh^2-dd@}\) (or completing the square, \({@(x-hh)^2@} = {@dd@}\)):</p>
\[ x = \dfrac{{@2*hh@} \pm \sqrt{@4*dd@}}{2} = {@hh@} \pm \sqrt{@dd@}. \]
<p>Substitute each \(x\)-value into the linear equation \(y = {@line@}\) to find the corresponding \(y\):</p>
<ul>
<li>\(x = {@hh+sqrt(dd)@}\) gives \(y = {@mm*(hh+sqrt(dd))+kk@}\);</li>
<li>\(x = {@hh-sqrt(dd)@}\) gives \(y = {@mm*(hh-sqrt(dd))+kk@}\).</li>
</ul>
<p>The two solutions are the points where the line meets the parabola:</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="The line y = {#line#} and the parabola y = {#para#}, meeting at two points.">
[[jsxgraph width="380px" height="320px"]]
(function() {
  var L = function(x){ return ({#mm#})*x + ({#kk#}); }, P = function(x){ return x*x + ({#pp#})*x + ({#qq#}); };
  var pts = [[{#float(hh+sqrt(dd))#},{#float(mm*(hh+sqrt(dd))+kk)#}],[{#float(hh-sqrt(dd))#},{#float(mm*(hh-sqrt(dd))+kk)#}]];
  var xs = pts.map(function(p){return p[0];}), ys = pts.map(function(p){return p[1];});
  var xmin = Math.min.apply(null, xs) - 2.5, xmax = Math.max.apply(null, xs) + 2.5;
  var ymin = Math.min(0, Math.min.apply(null, ys)), ymax = Math.max(0, Math.max.apply(null, ys));
  for (var t = xmin; t <= xmax; t += (xmax - xmin)/100) { var v = P(t); if (v < ymax + 6) ymax = Math.max(ymax, v); ymin = Math.min(ymin, v); }
  var pad = (ymax - ymin)*0.1 + 1;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[xmin, ymax + pad, xmax, ymin - pad], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('functiongraph', [P], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('functiongraph', [L], {strokeColor:'#e67e22', strokeWidth:2});
  for (var i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {
    b.create('point', pts[i], {name:'', size:4, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b'});
  }
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
